WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.860
I wonder if Haruka-chan is really back?

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.990
You got a call
from her teacher, didn't you?

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.530
She wouldn't go out of her way
to lie to us.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.980
Hey, Uchida-chan.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.240
- Huh?
- Geez.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.750
Yuu's there too, right?
What are they doing?

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.920
Who cares since Haruka is there.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.250
Those two are very suspicious.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.120
Looks like she's back.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.120
Thank goodness.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.520
Yes, this is Uchida.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.430
Yes, I understand.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.070
What's wrong?

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.210
I've been told to show up
at today's regular meeting.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.820
What? You gotta head back
to Tokyo right now?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.700
At the silver sky, the endless sky

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:11.030
I gazed together with you, without a word

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:17.210
Touching your back, with trembling fingers

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:22.640
I quietly ponder, as your profile looks up

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:28.680
I want to assure your smile, and the future ahead of you

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:35.020
Just standing and crying, I want to erase myself away

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.900
As I extend my hands, it is almost within my reach

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:46.950
This is no fantasy, possibilities are perhaps right by my side

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:52.790
Changing every sorrow into strength

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:58.960
Let's throw all limitations into the end of time

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.150
Just keeping you as my aspirations

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:07.300
Even in the driving wind

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:14.240
I'll still be pushing on ahead

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.900
Misekku kesta

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:27.820
Fortune. Will you save it for me, dear?

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.290
So like I said, he said he liked you!

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.820
What? You're wrong,
he said he liked you!

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.990
Tanaka spilled his heart out to you!

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.390
No way, a guy like him?!

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.520
That's right! Have you forgotten?

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.660
Yuup.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.330
Haruka! Oh, Haruka-chan!

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.490
Come on up!

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.800
Excuse me.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.840
Oh, I think we have company.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.490
Huh?

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.110
Welcome.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.500
Wow... Look at what
cute visitors we have.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.210
Oh, crap. It's Yuu's Mom.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.580
Asuka, we have guests!

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.390
Coming!

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.590
Hey, you're all here.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:21.260
If you want snacks,
they're in the usual place, okay?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.260
Thank you for always looking after Yuu.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.310
N-No, thank you for putting up with us.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.400
Isami-chan, you should
come over to play sometime.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.980
Whenever you come over, it makes
everything so jolly I just love it!

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:37.480
A... All right, I'll do that.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.570
Miyuki, get back over here!

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.380
Coming! See you.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:46.120
Hey, Asuka! Do you have any beer?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.550
I wonder what came over her?

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.820
It's impossible.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:49.750
Told you so.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.330
Yuu, what's going on with your mom?!

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.090
I think she's a little drunk.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.340
But that's okay, she looks
like she's enjoying herself.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.550
Well, yeah, but...

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.830
Never mind that! Haruka!

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.600
You haven't become involved
in something weird, have you?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.560
It... It's okay, Ai.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.560
Really?

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.100
Really, really.

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:17.710
You're making me worry.
Where the heck did you go?

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:19.280
Oh, somewhere...

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.490
Hey! You're trying to
hide things from me again!

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.120
Oh, yeah! Goto,
were you in the next room?

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.690
Huh? N-Not at all.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.080
I was in here the entire time.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.260
That's funny.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:35.760
When we got here, I could swear
I saw someone by the window upstairs.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.270
And that wasn't you?

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.270
Y-You're imagining things.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:44.310
This is the only room
being used on the 2nd floor.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.680
It's being used as a storage room, right?

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:47.600
Uh-huh.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:51.410
Then do you think...
that was a ghost?!

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.230
S-Stop it. I don't wanna hear
ghost stories in broad daylight.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:59.360
Hey, Haruka?
Has anything moved by itself?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.220
Have you heard any rapping noises?

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:03.130
Why does it always end up this way?

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.660
I'll drive out the ghost for you!

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.320
In preparation for
just such an occasion...

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.370
I carry one of these
with me wherever I go!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.950
This is so not possible.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:16.010
Evil spirit begone!

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:18.340
- I'm sorry!
- Evil spirit begone!

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.510
Please forgive me!
Please rest in peace!

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.140
Hey, this could get ugly.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.310
What'll I do?

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.110
What do you mean, get ugly?

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.220
You're hiding something,
aren't you, Haruka!

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.450
But it's...

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.720
No buts! Spill it, Haruka!

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.680
But I don't think you'd believe me.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.490
What are you talking about?

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:38.930
I'll believe anything
my best friend tells me, duh!

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.800
What? So it really is a ghost?

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:41.730
Oh, shut up.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.200
HOW DO YOU EXPECT ME
TO BELIEVE THAT?

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.200
Give me a break...

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.500
In what galaxy do you
expect anyone to believe...

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.740
you're harboring
a man from the future?!

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.410
That's more impossible than ghosts.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.110
People from the future
are just an illusion.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.850
So, whoever-he-is is really here?

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.750
Yup!

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.120
I can't believe you would let
someone like that into your home.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.250
It's all right.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.260
At any rate, I'll show him up
for what he really is.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.320
Ai?

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.790
Wait, Ai!

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.160
This is the room, right?

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.730
Hold on a second.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:18.600
What's with this guy? He's wearing
a black coat in the middle of summer!

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.640
There's no way this weirdo
is a man from the future!

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.960
It's really the ghost
in the black cape.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:24.860
You told them?

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.710
I'm sorry.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.870
You might have fooled Haruka,
but you won't fool me!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.370
Now tell us the truth!

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:36.280
Why did you come to her?
What are you after?!

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.490
He disappeared.

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:48.970
No way. That's impossible.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.570
Impossible...

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:04.940
Wh-What now?

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.240
That's pretty!

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.750
If you're really from the future...

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.660
Tell us what's happening 15 years from now!

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.140
Come on, we're waiting!

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:29.440
He can't talk about stuff like that.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.640
It would interfere with the past.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:35.310
I get it. It's the old
time warp story arch punch line!

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:37.050
Yuu, did you know about him?

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.080
Sorta.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.250
Why'd you keep it a secret from me?

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.820
I'm tight-lipped!
I would have kept your secret!

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.120
I think that's "impossible."

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:47.280
Excuse me?!

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:49.090
Take that!

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.590
Stop that, Isami!

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.860
It's your punishment!

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.230
- Hey, no horsing around!
- I can't breathe...

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.690
It's noogies for you!

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.740
I give... I give up Isami!

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.730
You little... Take this!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.750
What're you gonna do about Yuu?

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:06.610
I think he's playing with the others,
so I'll go on home by myself.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:09.250
Look after him for me.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:12.010
The kids can look after themselves.

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:14.410
That's true.

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:17.420
See you later, Miyuki.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:20.460
You should come to my house
the next time, Asuka.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.770
Absolutely!

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.560
I really thought he was a ghost.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.320
Get real!

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.410
I'm starting to like this.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:47.970
We've started to stabilize.
We're getting used to this dimension.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:53.460
Tobi, how long can we exist here for?

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.160
I can't tell.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:57.990
Oh, well. I feel good right now.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.560
It's no fun to think about the future.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.660
What do we do next?

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:10.150
That goes without saying.
We destroy the Dragon Torque.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.280
Except for that she's way too powerful.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.180
I don't wanna be thrown into
the dimensional ravine again.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:20.420
Then how?

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:23.420
We'll use the kid who's always with her.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:24.750
What?

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.260
Well, this is as far as we go.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.460
Yeah, later!

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:33.300
You shouldn't stay over
at Fujiwara's too long, Goto.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.960
It looks like it's gonna rain.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:36.870
I'm just gonna borrow a book.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:37.570
Bye!

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.830
- Later!
- See ya.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:39.890
Later.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.740
Still, don't you think we're weird?

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:47.480
Huh?

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.910
It's a man from the future!

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:54.020
We're harboring a strange man
wearing a weird getup.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.980
It's not normal to just
believe something like that.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:58.890
Yeah.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.030
See what I mean?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.180
Your mom's stopped
being as pesky as before.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:18.670
Sorta.

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:20.180
So no more studying for exams!

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.880
That's my problem, so...

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:36.700
There he is.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.890
You're right. That boy is Karasu.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:43.430
See? Isn't this a fun twist of fate...

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.760
being able to meet
his past face-to-face.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.680
Hey, there.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.480
How ya doin', kids?

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.690
It's you!

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:15.940
You remember me?

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.800
What's with this guy?

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:19.730
Isami, watch out.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.670
I only have business with this kid.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.160
Why the hell should I talk to you?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:29.000
The look in your eyes pisses me off.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:34.670
Would you like me to
gouge them out for you?

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.580
Stop it, Atori!

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:42.190
Tobi. What do you think you're doing?

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.990
Run, hurry up! Go on!

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.010
- Yuu!
- Right!

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:47.760
Why, you...

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:51.020
You can't interfere with this dimension
any more than you have already.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:53.700
Time-space is irreversible...

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.650
but it's impossible to predict
how the effects will...

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.140
Don't you patronize me.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.200
Atori...

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:05.700
If you get in my way again,
I'll kill you.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:12.180
Hurry!

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.210
Yuu!

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.460
Hi.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.710
This way!

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:26.600
Isami!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.770
- Let go of me, dammit!
- Isami!

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:33.850
So that's how it was. I heard
that you two were childhood friends...

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:36.690
This is perfect.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.910
Disappear, Fukuro.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.120
Stop it! Stop it!

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:44.410
Run for it, Yuu...

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:57.220
Why, you...

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.370
Damn. He got away.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.870
Hey, are you kids okay?

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.060
Uh-huh.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.680
Who are you?

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.570
Who, me? Well...

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.820
I guess you could say
I'm a broken-down old man.

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.360
Play nice now.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:35.330
Who was that?

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:37.970
He saved us.

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:39.070
But why?

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:42.370
I don't know. But...

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:47.550
Why do we have to split up?

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:52.750
I sent Fukuro on ahead with the mission
to secure the location of the Torque.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:56.390
Once its location is identified,
we will go in on one swoop.

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:58.810
Karasu is bound to show up!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.570
Fukuro will deal with Karasu.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.520
We will concentrate on the Dragon Torque.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:12.770
The irregular electromagnetic wave confirmed
at the prearranged experimentation site...

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.370
is predicted to be
from a quantum resonance.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.610
I already sent this to everyone here...

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:21.080
but it also appears on
the map of quantum potential...

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.980
I manufactured using
the observation data from the site.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.290
Since this event, there is
the possibility of...

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:31.520
A peculiar "place-site" being triggered in
that region.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:36.700
It is my personal opinion that
expanding the investigation area...

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:39.130
of the prearranged experimentation site...

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:42.400
and taking investigative measures
capable of comprehensive judgment...

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.540
concerning the abnormality
of the "place-site"...

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.320
Is the one and only way
to avoid the damages...

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.750
that may occur at the time
of the experiment.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:51.580
That is all.

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:57.290
I think that the expression "damages"
is inappropriate, Dr. Uchida.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.890
I wonder. It is my duty...

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:01.390
as a member of the Absolute Critical
Prevention Strategic Committee to...

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:03.090
A moment, Chairman.

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.190
Yes, Shinohara-kun?

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:07.060
Is the government really serious...

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:10.760
about putting a quantum transporter
into practical application?

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.420
I mean, at the rate we're going.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.980
Please explain yourself, Shinohara-kun.

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:18.460
Again...

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:23.410
Now listen. The entire world is
currently developing the technology...

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:26.450
to send large quantities
of data instantaneously.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.480
We're against the entire world.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:31.790
For all that, don't you think
that waiting for a survey...

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:35.390
of the effects on the surrounding region
that may or may not occur...

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:37.450
is a little inefficient?

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:39.660
Yes, but consider, Shinohara-kun...

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:43.060
There is an element of risk
in everything we do.

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:45.730
That's why we chose a site
located far away...

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:47.660
from Tokyo for the experiment, isn't it?

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.470
Don't get all bureaucratic on me...

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.970
just because it's a joint
military-civilian project!

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.300
My only concern is for
the safety of the region.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.740
Don't act high and mighty with me,
you scientist for hire!

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:03.150
I can perform a preliminary
investigation myself.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:06.790
I've got plenty of specialists
in quantum physics on the payroll.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.160
They're nothing special.

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:10.400
Just shut the hell up kid...

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.960
Did that old guy say something?

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:16.370
Silence!

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:22.470
The effects of a low pressure
system in the Sea of Okhotsk...

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:25.870
has resulted in a storm warning
for the lower city area.

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:26.440
It will let up...

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.540
The thunder is amazing.

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.440
I hope lighting doesn't strike the house.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.150
Wait, Karasu!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:48.980
Atori is after the Dragon Torque.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.600
I have to stop him.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.290
He's trying to destroy the Dragon Torque
along with this entire house.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.140
Negatively interfering with the Torque...

00:16:57.140 --> 00:17:00.500
means running the risk of
activating its enormous power.

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:04.290
That would accelerate the
destabilization of this dimension...

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.750
which could lead to the
obliteration of all dimensions.

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:09.310
Stop him, Karasu!

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:14.720
You got a phone call from Yuu, right?

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:15.520
Uh-huh.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:16.760
You kids going on a date?

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:18.490
Give me a break.

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:20.760
No? That's dull.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:24.810
Haruka, be careful. The guys
in the black capes are here again.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.330
Black capes?

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:29.480
It's the guy who attacked us
on the ropeway and one other.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.020
One other?

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:56.930
He's here alright.

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.910
Karasu...

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.240
Didn't think you'd be the first
to come out of hiding.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:20.010
Guess I can take care of
the Dragon Torque later.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:22.720
I think I'll start with you, Karasu.

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:28.670
I can't stop this.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:46.050
The weather's great.
Don't you think, Karasu?

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.240
Disappear!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.470
Die!

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:38.490
Mom?

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:41.460
Time has stopped.

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.630
Karasu? Karasu?

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.000
Where are you?

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.670
Disappear already!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.160
Kuina! Time has paused.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:07.630
Kuina!

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:10.520
Make contact with Fukuro, Kosagi.

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:15.020
This dimension is wavering more
than we estimated. Be careful!

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.770
Don't talk any more!

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.780
Must secure Dragon Torque...

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.700
It's there again.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:28.880
Dragon Torque...

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:35.420
I heard someone.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.300
Dragon Torque...

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.180
Dragon Torque.

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:49.600
You're...

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.140
I have come for you.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:55.100
Accompany me.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:05.740
Isami?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:08.290
You're the future Isami, aren't you?

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.860
Im...

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:11.790
Impossible!

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.790
This is an illusion!

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:21.190
Dammit. Hey, that hurts.

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:28.260
You piss me off.

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:35.810
Now die!

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:48.530
He disappeared?

00:21:48.860 --> 00:21:50.960
Karasu!

00:21:53.030 --> 00:21:54.500
Oh, damn it.

00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:01.240
Not yet... Not yet!

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.010
You're Isami, aren't you?

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:06.380
Stay back! Stay back...

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:09.010
Isami...

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:12.120
Karasu.

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:16.220
Move, Karasu.

00:22:16.220 --> 00:22:18.060
I will not let you have her.

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:20.230
Haruka?! Haruka?

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:22.030
She was right here a second ago.

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:24.030
Karasu...

00:22:24.270 --> 00:22:26.370
I will protect Haruka.

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:30.270
Until the day my body
disappears, I swear.

00:22:31.040 --> 00:22:32.600
Karasu...

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:36.500
Karasu, don't!

00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:39.000
You can't fight him!

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:41.800
That man is Isami, isn't it?

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:49.390
It started when you showed up.

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:52.760
You're the reason all this started.

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:55.020
Who are you?

00:22:55.930 --> 00:22:58.020
If it hadn't been for you...

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:30.350
A sleepless night

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:34.240
The sound of the second hand

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:41.170
The rumble of the
refrigerator in the air

00:23:42.070 --> 00:23:45.960
Just as the moon
through the blinds...

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:49.870
Waxes and wanes, someday...

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:56.460
The pain will change to warmth

00:23:56.460 --> 00:24:01.680
Boat of time...

00:24:02.270 --> 00:24:06.930
No matter where it flows...

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:13.060
Most likely we'll meet again

00:24:13.060 --> 00:24:16.700
From scars come the
footsteps of dawn

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:19.900
Rather than sighing,
they secretly...

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:26.010
come pouring down
on every new day

00:24:26.010 --> 00:24:30.550
No matter what sky it is

00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:45.210
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.210 --> 00:24:46.930
That summer day's dream.

00:24:47.810 --> 00:24:51.380
Do you seriously believe
in alternate worlds, Uchida-chan?

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:57.390
Who are you, mister?

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:02.100
We're still friends,
no matter how far apart we are.

00:25:04.090 --> 00:25:06.920
Next episode, Out of Sync.

00:25:07.260 --> 00:25:10.400
Is there anything I can do?
